1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,949
Water fills his helmet in orbit, and he nearly drowns.

2
00:00:03,067 --> 00:00:09,092
July 16, 2013. Luca Parmitano is outside the International Space Station.

3
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:11,248
About 250 miles above Earth.

4
00:00:11,367 --> 00:00:14,060
His suit has a water-cooling system, and it starts to leak.

5
00:00:14,167 --> 00:00:16,092
The water does not fall. It drifts.

6
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:18,842
It floats up over his face, and into his visor.

7
00:00:18,967 --> 00:00:21,664
He cannot see, and water is close to his face.

8
00:00:21,767 --> 00:00:23,793
Mission control tells him to come back in.

9
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:27,246
His partner, Chris Cassidy, guides him toward the airlock.

10
00:00:27,367 --> 00:00:30,010
Back inside the airlock, the danger is not over.

11
00:00:30,133 --> 00:00:33,119
NASA calls off the spacewalk and investigates the leak.

12
00:00:33,233 --> 00:00:35,595
He nearly drowned in a spacesuit, in orbit.

13
00:00:35,700 --> 00:00:39,500
The most dangerous ocean an astronaut can face is inside his own helmet.
